Cyberphone
Modifications Copyright (c) 2026 Yshawn6720

Cyberphone is a modified version (fork) of FFXIV-Aetherphone, based on
upstream tag v1.3.3.0 (commit 4b72228612b0616a41640fc3c846114f5104ab00,
https://github.com/XeldarAlz/FFXIV-Aetherphone). It is not Aetherphone, is not
endorsed by its authors, and does not connect to the official Aethernet
servers. Report problems to https://github.com/Yshawn6720/Cyberphone, not to
the Aetherphone project. The modified version is licensed under the same
terms, AGPL-3.0-or-later.

Modifications (AGPL-3.0 section 5(a)), first made 2026-10-21:

- 2026-10-21  Ported to the Traditional Chinese client's Dalamud (API 13,
              .NET 9): SDK downgrade, Dalamud/Lumina/ClientStructs API
              differences, net9 test project.
- 2026-10-21  Official Aethernet hosts blocked before DNS resolution by
              src/Aetherphone/Core/Net/OfficialHostGuard.cs, the only place
              that creates HTTP clients and WebSockets; default service base
              URL points at a reserved .invalid name. Guarded by
              src/Aetherphone.Tests/OfflineGuaranteeTests.cs.
- 2026-10-21  Aethernet-only apps (social, chat, calls, casino, coin,
              feedback, polls, Muster, Yellow Pages), Strats and announcements
              hidden; account sign-in removed from setup and Settings; links
              to upstream community and donation pages removed.
- 2026-10-21  Renamed to Cyberphone in player-visible text (all nine
              languages), slash commands /cyberphone and /cphone, plugin
              manifest, plugin file Cyberphone.dll and InternalName
              Cyberphone. The assembly name and code namespaces remain
              "Aetherphone" for now because the bundled SixLabors licence is
              scoped to that assembly name.
- 2026-10-21  App icons, plugin icon and emblem regenerated from Phosphor
              Icons (MIT) duotone glyphs in Cyberphone's own style; seasonal
              icon variants dropped.
- 2026-10-21  Removed assets that need their owners' permission: the 58
              contributed artwork phone cases (src/Aetherphone/Cases/*.png)
              and the Rolladeck partner mark (Icons/rolladeck.png).
- 2026-10-21  Added a Traditional Chinese (Taiwan) language with Taiwan
              client language detection; the shared CJK font now draws the
              game's own Axis glyphs; Hunts is hidden on the Traditional
              Chinese client, which Faloop does not serve; realtime signals
              are no longer sent while Aethernet is off.
- 2026-10-21  Watch parties run through a self-hosted relay instead of
              Aethernet: relay server in server/ (Cloudflare Worker and
              Durable Objects, see docs/self-hosting-relay.md); MogCast
              settings for the relay address and invite code; the party tab
              appears only when both are set, and the plugin connects only
              when a party is started or joined. Host heartbeat relaxed from
              8 to 30 seconds. Party features the relay does not implement
              are hidden while using it.
- 2026-10-22  The in-world video screen is drawn from Dalamud's UI draw
              callback instead of a DirectX Present hook, so turning the
              plugin off and on leaves no hook behind in the game's present
              call; the screen now hides whenever Dalamud hides plugin
              windows. ScreenPainter logs why a frame was not drawn, only
              when the reason changes.
- 2026-10-22  Music Jam runs through the same self-hosted relay: a JamRoom
              Durable Object in server/, the shared relay address and invite
              code from MogCast settings, and a connection only while a Jam
              is started or joined. Host heartbeat relaxed from 8 to 30
              seconds; the relay ends the Jam when the host leaves.
- 2026-10-22  The MogCast relay party regains join approval, queue
              suggestions, reactions and removing a member. The relay holds
              newcomers until the host approves, passes suggestions to the
              host and the answer back to the author, forwards reactions on
              a separate per-member budget (the plugin sends at most 4 at
              once, then 1 a second) and closes a removed member's
              connection; the plugin does not reconnect after being removed
              or declined. Nearby parties stay unavailable.
- 2026-10-22  Announcements and the in-game events in Calendar come back
              through the self-hosted relay: server/content holds both as
              static JSON that the Worker serves behind the invite code, with
              an ETag and no Durable Object. The plugin keeps a local copy,
              checks again at most every 6 hours and only when Announcements
              or Calendar is shown, sends no announcement notifications, and
              keeps Announcements hidden with no request while no relay is
              set.
- 2026-10-22  Games "Play together" comes back through the self-hosted relay
              as invite-based rooms: a GameRoom Durable Object in server/
              referees Uno, Chess, Connect Four and Broadside itself, keeps
              hands and fleets private, and closes the room when the host
              leaves. The plugin connects only while a room is created or
              joined, sends one move at a time under its own budget, and
              hides 8-Ball Pool, Moogle War, Mini Golf, Lucky Draw, the
              public room list, matchmaking and leaderboards while on the
              relay.
- 2026-10-22  Voice calls come back as invite-based call rooms in a new
              Calls tab in Linkpearl: a CallRoom Durable Object in server/
              forwards Opus frames between up to 4 members without decoding
              or storing them, and only runs where CALLS_ENABLED is on (the
              Docker compose setup; the Workers configuration keeps it off
              and answers 403). The plugin connects only while a room is
              open, closes the link as soon as the call is left, never
              retries a server without calls, and keeps direct dialing,
              ringing, the online list, the Control Center toggle, Spotlight
              and the call command hidden.

